{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Python code to GNU C++11 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following Python 3 code to GNU C++11 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original Python 3 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n<your_rewritten_code_5>\nimport sys\nfrom math import factorial\n\ninput = sys.stdin.readline\n\ndef A(n, k):\n    return factorial(n) // factorial(n - k)\n\ndef solve():\n    n, mod = map(int, input().split())\n    if n == 1:\n        print(0)\n        return\n    \n    z = [1]\n    total = 0\n    \n    for i in range(2, n + 1):\n        # Compute new_z array\n        new_z = [0] * ((i - 1) * i // 2 + 1)\n        \n        # Compute d array (suffix sums of z)\n        d = [0] * (len(z) + 1)\n        for idx in reversed(range(len(z))):\n            d[idx] = (d[idx + 1] + z[idx]) % mod\n        \n        # Fill new_z using d\n        for w in range(len(new_z)):\n            L = max(0, w + 1 - i)\n            R = min(len(z) - 1, w)\n            new_z[w] = (d[L] - d[R + 1]) % mod\n        \n        # Compute e and f arrays\n        e = [0] * (len(d) + 1)\n        f = [0] * (len(d) + 1)\n        for idx in range(len(e) - 1):\n            e[idx + 1] = (e[idx] + d[idx]) % mod\n            f[idx + 1] = (f[idx] - idx * d[idx]) % mod\n        \n        # Compute bbb\n        bbb = 0\n        R = len(z)\n        \n        # First segment\n        for jj in range(max(0, len(z) - i), len(z) - 2):\n            L = jj + 2\n            bbb = (bbb + ((e[R] - e[L]) * (i + 1 + jj) + (f[R] - f[L])) * z[jj]) % mod\n        \n        # Second segment\n        for jj in range(len(z) - i):\n            L = jj + 2\n            R2 = i + jj\n            bbb = (bbb + ((e[R2 + 1] - e[L]) * (i + 1 + jj) + (f[R2 + 1] - f[L])) * z[jj]) % mod\n        \n        # Update total\n        total = (total + bbb * A(n, n - i)) % mod\n        z = new_z\n    \n    print(total % mod)\n\nsolve()\n</your_rewritten_code_5>\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <algorithm>\nusing namespace std;\n\nlong long factorial(int n) {\n    long long result = 1;\n    for (int i = 2; i <= n; i++) {\n        result *= i;\n    }\n    return result;\n}\n\nlong long A(int n, int k) {\n    return factorial(n) / factorial(n - k);\n}\n\nint main() {\n    int n, mod;\n    cin >> n >> mod;\n    \n    if (n == 1) {\n        cout << 0 << endl;\n        return 0;\n    }\n    \n    vector<long long> z = {1};\n    long long total = 0;\n    \n    for (int i = 2; i <= n; i++) {\n        // Compute new_z array\n        int new_z_size = (i - 1) * i / 2 + 1;\n        vector<long long> new_z(new_z_size, 0);\n        \n        // Compute d array (suffix sums of z)\n        vector<long long> d(z.size() + 1, 0);\n        for (int idx = (int)z.size() - 1; idx >= 0; idx--) {\n            d[idx] = (d[idx + 1] + z[idx]) % mod;\n        }\n        \n        // Fill new_z using d\n        for (int w = 0; w < new_z_size; w++) {\n            int L = max(0, w + 1 - i);\n            int R = min((int)z.size() - 1, w);\n            new_z[w] = (d[L] - d[R + 1]) % mod;\n            if (new_z[w] < 0) new_z[w] += mod;\n        }\n        \n        // Compute e and f arrays\n        vector<long long> e(d.size() + 1, 0);\n        vector<long long> f(d.size() + 1, 0);\n        for (int idx = 0; idx < (int)d.size(); idx++) {\n            e[idx + 1] = (e[idx] + d[idx]) % mod;\n            f[idx + 1] = (f[idx] - (long long)idx * d[idx]) % mod;\n        }\n        \n        // Compute bbb\n        long long bbb = 0;\n        int R = z.size();\n        \n        // First segment\n        for (int jj = max(0, (int)z.size() - i); jj < (int)z.size() - 2; jj++) {\n            int L = jj + 2;\n            long long term = ((e[R] - e[L]) * (i + 1 + jj) + (f[R] - f[L])) % mod;\n            bbb = (bbb + term * z[jj]) % mod;\n        }\n        \n        // Second segment\n        for (int jj = 0; jj < (int)z.size() - i; jj++) {\n            int L = jj + 2;\n            int R2 = i + jj;\n            long long term = ((e[R2 + 1] - e[L]) * (i + 1 + jj) + (f[R2 + 1] - f[L])) % mod;\n            bbb = (bbb + term * z[jj]) % mod;\n        }\n        \n        // Update total\n        bbb = (bbb % mod + mod) % mod; // Ensure non-negative\n        total = (total + bbb * A(n, n - i)) % mod;\n        z = new_z;\n    }\n    \n    total = (total % mod + mod) % mod; // Ensure non-negative\n    cout << total << endl;\n    \n    return 0;\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.75\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.00012432756193447858, -4.768360213347478e-06, -7.152555099310121e-07, -0.0011328000109642744, 0.0, -0.00021181246847845614, -4.529942543740617e-06, -4.529942543740617e-06, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -4.2914423829643056e-05, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -0.0011713793501257896, -1.5497195136049413e-06, -0.030944691970944405, -0.026301492005586624, -0.42874133586883545, -2.2053474822314456e-05, -2.264974000354414e-06, -1.0728830375228426e-06, -0.002289414405822754, -1.1324817933200393e-05, -0.0012753218179568648, -0.5278955698013306, -8.940656698541716e-06, -1.0728830375228426e-06, 0.0, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -0.005248932633548975, -1.07287787614041e-05,